      "severity": "HIGH",
      "title": "2025/26 is not a globally untouched holdout",
      "detail": "The season has already been examined in prior model comparison, tuning, calibration and error-slice experiments. It can remain a walk-forward fold but must not be called a project-wide untouched final holdout."
    },
    {
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "title": "Auto target mode can fall back to proxy PDK",
      "detail": "Production selects official labels only when at least 1,000 finite labels exist; otherwise it silently chooses target_pdk. Official-target experiments should assert label provenance and fail closed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "title": "Rolling features sort only by date",
      "detail": "The production rolling builder sorts by GAME_DATE without a game/time tie-break. shift(1) is safe only when each player has unique dates; dataset duplicate counts are reported below."
    },
    {
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "title": "The main GW1 trainer is still prior-season-only",
      "detail": "The production run_train opening-round branch loads player_game_logs_<feature_season>.parquet and builds its primary training matrix from that season. The multi-season V3 dataset is used by a separate historical model path, not as the main supervised training matrix. Therefore the requested 2018/19–2024/25 multi-season training policy is not yet the production trainer's policy."
    },
    {
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "title": "Official labels and rolling PDK features have different provenance",
      "detail": "attach_official_pdk_labels adds PDK_OFFICIAL_VALID without replacing the original PDK column. build_feature_matrix derives target_pdk from PDK and rolling PDK features from that same column; when train_models selects target_pdk_official as y, the labels are official but PDK-history predictors may remain proxy-derived. This is not future leakage, but it is a feature/target provenance mismatch worth measuring before integration."
    },
    {
      "severity": "INFO",
      "title": "Historical certified target set spans 2020/21 onward",
      "detail": "The existing V3 dataset has 112,178 rows from 2020/21–2025/26; 93,766 rows are from 2020/21–2024/25. Earlier two seasons can provide verified NBA history, not certified PDK supervised labels."
    }
  ],
  "recommended_next_steps": [
    "For the requested 2018/19–2024/25 time span, use verified NBA boxscores from 2018/19–2019/20 as prior features, but train supervised PDK labels on certified 2020/21–2024/25 rows unless authoritative labels are recovered.",
    "Use expanding-origin folds inside 2020/21–2024/25 for model, feature, rookie and calibration selection; treat 2025/26 as a historical final fold with explicit project-wide holdout caveat.",
    "Make player/date uniqueness and lag-integrity checks hard assertions for each dataset build.",
    "For official-target experiments, require a minimum certified label count and fail closed rather than silently switching to proxy labels.",
    "Before production integration, decide whether the primary GW1 trainer should consume the multi-season certified PDK dataset; compare it in chronological folds against the existing prior-season-only trainer.",
    "Measure official-PDK history features versus proxy-PDK history features in walk-forward validation; do not assume that changing the historical features helps without out-of-sample evidence.",
    "Keep player PDK model validation separate from lineup/coach/transfer evaluation, which requires authentic pre-match snapshots and fixture-linked official results."
  ]
